THIRD-PARTY DATA
================

The diagnostic trouble code catalog in internal/dtc/data/ is not original
work. It is assembled by "cargo import" from the following datasets.

  Wal33D/dtc-database
  https://github.com/Wal33D/dtc-database
  Copyright (c) 2024 Wal33D (Waleed Judah)
  MIT License

  todrobbins/dtcdb
  https://github.com/todrobbins/dtcdb
  Copyright (c) 2013 trobbins
  MIT License

Both are MIT licensed and compatible with this project's terms.

A note on scope: an MIT grant from a dataset's maintainer covers their
compilation. It does not settle the rights to the underlying definitions,
which these projects gathered from sources they do not identify. The
authoritative definitions live in SAE J2012, a paid standard, and every
freely available list is downstream of it. Manufacturer-specific codes are
more restricted still, as J2012 reserves the ranges but the meanings belong
to each marque's service documentation.

Treat the catalog as a helpful index rather than an authority. Descriptions
carry their source through to the display, manufacturer codes are tagged
with the make that defined them, and an unmatched code falls back to what
its encoding proves rather than to a guess.


